  "term": "captivity",
  "definition": "Captivity is the state of being kept in a restricted enclosure rather than a natural habitat. In a learning and behavior context, this change in environment can markedly shift an animal’s usual behavior, sometimes leading to abnormal repetitive actions, changes in feeding, and greater responsiveness to people.",
